@startuml 07-node-executor-extension
skinparam backgroundColor white
title Rastok — semantic ownership (not a Rust API inventory)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty methods
top to bottom direction

abstract class Node {
  path; typed ports
  instance; lifetime; Closing
}
class Graph {
  boundary; children; wiring; lexical val
  no application mailbox, var or handler
}
abstract class Executor {
  instance mailbox; semantic state
  atomic transactions; ordered emissions
}
class Operator {
  private var; one Dispatch per trigger
}
class Connector {
  one exact versioned Contract
  no DSL handler or var
}
class Contract {
  ports; settings; exchange profile
  cardinality; terminal cases; effect visibility
}
abstract class Extension
class App {
  exactly one root Graph; no manager
}
class Loop {
  entry; terminals; fuel / measure; delay
  Loop.state; resolved exhaustion target
  contributes no port
}
class Retry {
  outbound Call; same prepared request
  attempts; terminal cases; delay
  no ports, commands or new terminal
}
class "Saga (deferred)" as Saga
class Manager {
  bounded journal-owned recurrence
  Loop commands / Retry held attempts
  temporal admission; no PhysicalEdge
}
class Driver {
  physical resource state
  typed external events; no journal writes
}

Node <|-- Graph
Node <|-- Executor
Executor <|-- Operator
Executor <|-- Connector
Graph "0..1 parent" o-- "0..* children" Node
Node "1 owner" *-- "0..* canonical" Extension
Connector "*" --> "1" Contract
Connector --> Driver : bound before execution
Extension <|-- App
Extension <|-- Loop
Extension <|-- Retry
Extension <|-- Saga
Loop *-- Manager
Retry *-- Manager
Manager ..> Node : owner address / generation

note left of Node
instance.stop closes the current generation.
child.instance.stop targets a direct child.
Recorded commands, never spatial ports.
end note
note bottom of Graph
Generic lifecycle records may name a Graph.
They are not Graph application transactions.
end note
note bottom of Loop
Hosts: Operator, Graph, finite outbound Call.
Exhaustion is LoopExpired on existing err,
custom terminal, or the Call's extended exit.
Commands are not ports or spatial edges.
end note
note bottom of Retry
All attempts recorded; only the final one delivered.
Backoff starts at the unsealed Call closure instant.
Idempotence is a plan guarantee, not a CallOpen field.
end note
note bottom of Driver
Process job: finite Call.
Process service: resident Session per instance.
Session frames are fresh admitted INGRESS facts.
end note
@enduml
